The market clearing analysis for the base and counterfactual scenarios has been performed using a DC-OPF model with reserve co-optimization. The results indicate that the transmission constraint on the line connecting bus 64 to bus 1501 was a significant driver of congestion in the base case. Increasing its thermal capacity by 20% relieved this congestion, leading to a reduction in total system cost of approximately \$3,878.53 per hour and a substantial decrease in Locational Marginal Prices (LMPs) at the most affected buses.

The complete analysis results are available in the `report.json` file.

```json
{
  "base_case": {
    "total_cost_dollars_per_hour": 2965637.91,
    "lmp_by_bus": [ ... ],
    "reserve_mcp_dollars_per_MWh": 0.0,
    "binding_lines": [
      {
        "from": 64,
        "to": 1501,
        "flow_MW": -312.0,
        "limit_MW": 312.0
      },
      ...
    ]
  },
  "counterfactual": {
    "total_cost_dollars_per_hour": 2961759.38,
    "lmp_by_bus": [ ... ],
    "reserve_mcp_dollars_per_MWh": 0.0,
    "binding_lines": [ ... ]
  },
  "impact_analysis": {
    "cost_reduction_dollars_per_hour": 3878.53,
    "buses_with_largest_lmp_drop": [
      {"bus": 64, "base_lmp": 1235561.64, "cf_lmp": 378986.64, "delta": -856575.0},
      {"bus": 629, "base_lmp": 897072.91, "cf_lmp": 377329.15, "delta": -519743.76},
      {"bus": 676, "base_lmp": 869903.1, "cf_lmp": 377656.78, "delta": -492246.32}
    ],
    "congestion_relieved": true
  }
}
```
